<key_info>Task: Fix CWE-93 CRLF injection vulnerability in /app/bottle.py, create report.jsonl, verify with pytest.

VULNERABILITY IDENTIFIED:
- CWE-93: CRLF Injection in HTTP headers
- Location: _hval() function (line 1565) and _hkey() function (line 1560)
- Issue: No validation of control characters (\r, \n, \0) in header names/values
- Impact: Allows HTTP header injection attacks

FAILING TEST:
- test/test_environ.py::TestResponse::test_prevent_control_characters_in_headers
- Tests HeaderDict methods: append, replace, __setitem__, setdefault
- Expects ValueError when header names contain \n, \r, \n\r, or \0

SOLUTION:
1. Modify _hval() to validate and reject control characters in header values
2. Modify _hkey() to validate and reject control characters in header names
3. Both should raise ValueError when control chars detected

Next: Read test to understand exact requirements, fix _hval() and _hkey(), create report.jsonl, verify with pytest</key_info>
